Subject: Remove piped python3 example blocked by Tirith

Why: The platform image build runs Tirith (`deploy/docker/check_skill_commands.py`) over every fenced shell block in shipped skills, and Tirith blocks example `(b)` (`<read-only export command> | python3 scripts/trace_logs.py ... --data-path -`) with a HIGH `pipe_to_interpreter` finding. Removing both the piped example and the accompanying `--data-path -` / stdin prose in `SKILL.md` and `references/log-sources.md` avoids the Tirith block and prevents agents from piping exports into `python3` at runtime while preserving the file-based `--data-path <file-or-dir>` workflow.
Local-Issue: none (adoption of gke-kueue-troubleshooting from google/skills)
Eval-Case: kueue-troubleshooting-mixed-flavor-tas-probe
Upstream-Issue: none filed yet
Retire-When: upstream removes the piped `| python3` example from `references/log-sources.md` or Tirith exempts local script pipes

